inithooks (2.3.6+keel11) trixie; urgency=medium

  * dialog_wrapper: get_password() offers a generated password
    (Keel-Linux/inithooks#23), from turnkeylinux/inithooks#71 by Marcos
    Mendez, as revised in #74. A menu comes first, "Generate (recommended)"
    or "Manual". Generate draws 20 characters with the secrets module from
    59: letters and digits without 0 O o 1 l I, and - . ~, which need no
    escaping in a shell word, a URL, a PHP string or the KEY=value line
    the database and WordPress hooks read; the first and last are a letter
    or a digit. The password is shown in bold reverse video and returned
    only once the operator answers "Saved"; "New" shows another. It meets
    the caller's pass_req, min_complexity and blacklist, which Manual still
    enforces as before. offer_generate=False keeps the old prompt alone.
    From the review of #74: a length under 12 is refused, blacklisted
    characters are left out, and only attributes are used, not colors.
  * dialog_wrapper: a password never reaches /var/log/dialog.log. At
    DEBUG (DIALOG_DEBUG) the wrapper logged each widget's answer, so a
    typed password was written there; a password box's value is now
    redacted, and the text shown, which carries a generated password, was
    already.
  * dialog_wrapper: the widgets draw on the controlling terminal when
    stdout is not one. bin/dbpass.py (keel-mariadb) and bin/wordpress.py
    (keel-wordpress) print KEY=value for a hook that reads it through a
    pipe, so the screen went into the pipe: the operator saw nothing,
    dialog failed and the first boot hung in 35mysqlpass.
  * dialog_wrapper: ESC never skips a password or another value. On a
    menu, an input box or a password box, and on every dialog of
    get_password(), ESC shows the dialog again; "really quit?" stays on
    the widgets that return a bare code, elsewhere. A quit inside
    get_password() had ended setpass.py with status 0 and no chpasswd, and
    30rootpass carried on with the password unchanged.
  * dialog_wrapper: when nothing can be generated (gen_length under 12, or
    a blacklist that leaves no letter or digit), Generate falls back to
    Manual instead of raising. The password dialogs compute their height
    at the width they are drawn with, counting visible characters.

